  "title": "11 to 20",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**১১–২০** each have their own shape — there is no simple 'teen' rule, so practise by ear:\n\n**এগারো, বারো, তেরো, চৌদ্দ, পনেরো, ষোলো, সতেরো, আঠারো, উনিশ, বিশ**\n\nSome hints still help: **তেরো** echoes **তিন**, **পনেরো** echoes **পাঁচ**, **আঠারো** echoes **আট**, and **উনিশ** literally means 'one short of twenty' (**বিশ**).\n\nAge: **আমার বয়স বিশ** — literally 'my age (is) twenty'. Ask with **তোমার বয়স কি সতেরো?** 'Are you seventeen?'. Asking someone's age is quite normal in Bangladesh, but with elders it's polite not to.\n\nYou'll see these numbers written in **Bengali digits** (১১, ১২ …) everywhere — that's the next lesson.",
